<title>NETHERLANDS: DANISH REFERENDUM LIKELY ON IGC OUTCOME - MINISTER.</title>
<headline>DANISH REFERENDUM LIKELY ON IGC OUTCOME - MINISTER.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish Economy Minister Marianne Jelved said on Monday it was very likely that Denmark would need to hold a referendum on the outcome of European Union reform talks due to be concluded at the June 16-17 summit in Amsterdam.</p>
<p>Asked how likely it was that Denmark would need a referendum on the outcome of the EU's inter-governmental conference (IGC), she told Reuters: &quot;Ninety nine percent.... but we have to wait to see the final text.</p>
<p>Jelved said such a referendum could be held in February-March next year.</p>
</text>
